    1. Pick grid size in 16-20 x 16-19.
    2. Pick 1-3 rectangles with sizes 6-13 x 6-13; place them on the grid with >=1 cell gap between pairs, allowing grid-edge contact.
    3. For each rectangle, pick 3-5 distinct non-zero colors for layers.
    4. Build layers outside-in. For each non-innermost layer, pick uniform thickness 1 or 2. Ensure remaining interior after peeling is >=1x1 and can accommodate remaining layers (at least 2*remaining_layers-1 in each dimension).
    5. The innermost layer fills whatever remains.
    6. Paint layers onto the rectangle region. Fill background with 0.
